I just had a quick look at this, and it appears the following patch changes the current behaviour to match the documentation.

```diff
diff --git a/src/nvim/mark.c b/src/nvim/mark.c
index 6453c41..addf16d 100644
--- a/src/nvim/mark.c
+++ b/src/nvim/mark.c
@@ -135,7 +135,17 @@ int setmark_pos(int c, pos_T *pos, int fnum)
     return FAIL;
   if (islower(c)) {
     i = c - 'a';
-    RESET_FMARK(curbuf->b_namedm + i, *pos, curbuf->b_fnum);
+    buf_T *buf = curbuf;
+    if (fnum != curbuf->b_fnum) {
+        buf = firstbuf;
+        while (buf != NULL && buf->b_fnum != fnum) {
+            buf = buf->b_next;
+        }
+        if (buf == NULL) {
+            return FAIL;
+        }
+    }
+    RESET_FMARK(buf->b_namedm + i, *pos, fnum);
     return OK;
   }
   if (isupper(c)) {
```

I'm not sure whether you guys feel the behaviour or documentation should be changed, but looked for this based on the title change.

There are only two places where the function `setmark_pos()` is called, one is from `setmark()` where the `fnum` argument is hard-coded to be of the current buffer, and the other from the `setpos()` function itself, so I doubt this will have adverse effects.
I ran the test suite and everything seemed fine.

I can add a test for this specific behaviour if needed -- I wasn't quite sure where to put it or whether having tests for every vimL function is thought of as overkill.

> whether having tests for every vimL function is thought of as overkill.

Not at all. The more the merrier.

@chrisbra This seems like a change Vim would want as well.
